=== vocabulary ===
An order is a kind of thing.
An order item is a kind of thing.
A customer is a kind of person.
An invoice is a kind of artifact.
A payment is a kind of event.
A product is a kind of thing.
A shipment is a kind of event.
A purchase order is a kind of artifact.
A warehouse is a kind of thing.
A period is a kind of thing.
A trigger phrase is a kind of thing.

An order has a number, a status, a total amount, a customer id, and an updated at.
An order item has a sku, a quantity, and a status.
A customer has a customer id, a name, and a status.
An invoice has a number, a status, a balance, a due date, and an updated at.
A payment has a reference, a status, and an amount.
A product has a sku, a status, a quantity on hand, a reorder point, and an updated at.
A shipment has a tracking number, a status, and an updated at.
A purchase order has a number, a status, and an updated at.
A warehouse has a name and a region.
A period has a name, a status, and a closed at.
A trigger phrase has a text.

Definition: an order is open if its status is "open".
Definition: an order is blocked if its status is "blocked".
Definition: an order is fulfilled if its status is "fulfilled".
Definition: an invoice is unpaid if its balance is more than 0.
Definition: an invoice is overdue if its due date is within the last 1 days.
Definition: a product is short if its quantity on hand is less than its reorder point.
Definition: a purchase order is pending if its status is "pending".

Fulfillment relates an order to a shipment.
Fulfillment is read via the shipment.create tool.
Invoicing relates an order to an invoice.
Invoicing is read via the invoice.create tool.
Collection relates an invoice to a payment.
Collection is read via the payment.collect tool.
Replenishment relates a product to a purchase order.
Replenishment is read via the purchase_order.create tool.

The verb to fulfill (it fulfills, it is fulfilled) means the fulfillment relation.
The verb to invoice (it invoices, it is invoiced) means the invoicing relation.
The verb to collect (it collects, it is collected) means the collection relation.
The verb to replenish (it replenishes, it is replenished) means the replenishment relation.

To fetch open orders:
  bind orders = invoke order.list with status = "open".

To fetch unpaid invoices:
  bind invoices = invoke invoice.list with status = "unpaid".

To fetch short products:
  bind products = invoke product.list with status = "short".

To reserve inventory for an order:
  invoke inventory.reserve with order = the order.

To create an invoice for an order:
  bind invoice = invoke invoice.create with order = the order.

To collect payment for an invoice:
  bind payment = invoke payment.collect with invoice = the invoice.

To ship an order:
  bind shipment = invoke shipment.create with order = the order.

To create a purchase order for a product:
  bind purchase order = invoke purchase_order.create with product = the product.

To cancel an order:
  invoke order.cancel with order = the order.

To close the accounting period:
  invoke period.close.

=== tools ===
List Orders
===========
-- List orders by status.
~ order.list(status: String) : List

List Invoices
=============
-- List invoices by status.
~ invoice.list(status: String) : List

List Products
=============
-- List products by status.
~ product.list(status: String) : List

Reserve Inventory
=================
-- Reserve inventory for an order.
~ inventory.reserve(order: Order) : Boolean

Create Invoice
==============
-- Create an invoice for an order.
~ invoice.create(order: Order) : Invoice

Collect Payment
===============
-- Collect payment for an invoice.
~ payment.collect(invoice: Invoice) : Payment

Create Shipment
===============
-- Ship an order.
~ shipment.create(order: Order) : Shipment

Create Purchase Order
=====================
-- Create replenishment purchase order.
~ purchase_order.create(product: Product) : PurchaseOrder

Cancel Order
============
-- Cancel an order.
~ order.cancel(order: Order) : Boolean

Close Period
============
-- Close the accounting period.
~ period.close() : Boolean
